\subsubsection{Period $N = 58$}
The period $N=58$ is realised by $361$ parameter sets across $2\\times2$, $2\\times3$, $2\\times4$, $2\\times6$, $3\\times3$, $3\\times4$, $3\\times6$, $4\\times4$, $4\\times6$, $6\\times6$. The reflection parameters take values in $\{$0.0616$, $0.1763$, $0.2351$, $0.2658$, $0.3149$, $0.3662$, $0.4191$, $0.4729$, $0.4883$, $0.5271$, $0.5809$, $0.6306$, $0.6338$, $0.6851$, $0.7745$, $0.8237$, $0.8630$, $0.9134$\}$, and the phase parameters in $\{$0.0000\pi$, $1.0000\pi$, $2.0000\pi$\}$. This is one of the longest periods in the classification,
and is confined to a small number of tori whose revival
period sets intersect at a large common value.
